WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.820
Did you know that these Hip Hop&nbsp;
legends went to high school together?

00:00:02.820 --> 00:00:08.040
Jay-Z, Biggie Smalls, and Busta Rhymes&nbsp;
all attended George Westinghouse Career&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:08.040 --> 00:00:09.840
and Technical High School in downtown Brooklyn.

00:00:09.840 --> 00:00:13.560
Busta Rhymes and Jay-Z actually&nbsp;
had a rap battle in the cafeteria.

00:00:13.560 --> 00:00:17.040
Both Jay and Busta admitted&nbsp;
that Jay-Z won the battle.

00:00:17.700 --> 00:00:20.220
Busta Rhymes said that at the time&nbsp;
they were experimenting with speed rap,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:20.220 --> 00:00:22.560
which took less influence from New York hip-hop

00:00:22.560 --> 00:00:27.240
and more influence from Jamaican Dancehall&nbsp;
artists like Lt. Stitchie and Papa San.

00:00:27.240 --> 00:00:34.200
When the two high schoolers faced off in&nbsp;
the lunch room, Busta Rhymes said he had&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:34.200 --> 00:00:38.040
just started experimenting with speed&nbsp;
rap, and Jay-Z had already mastered it.

00:00:38.040 --> 00:00:42.180
But today it’s Busta Rhymes that’s famous&nbsp;
for his fast verses on his hit songs.

00:00:42.180 --> 00:00:44.580
So we think it would be fun&nbsp;
to see their rematch today.

